WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.590
Stock, profit, and one workbook for your whole business.

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.830
This is the video for Module 4 of Excel and Google Sheets for Small Business.

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:21.920
Stock is often the biggest amount of money a small trader has tied up. An inventory sheet tells you what you have, what it is worth, and what to reorder before customers find empty shelves.

4
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:27.820
It also feeds prices into your sales log, so you stop typing them by hand.

5
00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:36.620
Then a profit report answers the question every partner or lender asks. Did the business actually make money this month?

6
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:45.890
On a Products tab, give each product a short unique code, like P01, then its name, cost price and selling price.

7
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.200
Then type the opening stock, the stock you bought in, and the units sold.

8
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.390
Closing stock is opening stock, plus stock in, minus sold.

9
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:07.710
Set a reorder level for each product. If closing stock falls to that level, IF shows the word Reorder. Your sheet becomes an automatic shopping list.

10
00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.010
Stock value is closing stock times cost price.

11
00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:23.310
For example, Funke has 6 detergents left, and her reorder level is 8, so it says Reorder. Her stock on hand is worth 80250 naira at cost.

12
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:40.300
On your Sales tab, type just the product code, and let a lookup fetch the price. XLOOKUP finds the code in the Code column and returns the selling price from the same row. If the code is P03, it returns 3300.

13
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:48.610
If your Excel is 2019 or older, use VLOOKUP. The code must be in the first column of the table.

14
00:01:48.960 --> 00:02:01.040
And always finish with FALSE. Leaving it out can quietly return the wrong product's price. If you see hash N A, the code was not found. Check for a letter O typed instead of a zero.

15
00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:14.770
Now profit. Sales is the money earned from selling. Cost of goods sold is what the goods you actually sold cost you: opening stock value, plus purchases, minus closing stock value.

16
00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:23.240
Why not sales minus purchases? Because if you stock up heavily, the month looks like a loss even though the goods are still on your shelves.

17
00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:32.920
Gross profit is sales minus cost of goods. Net profit takes away running costs too, like rent, transport, data and power.

18
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:39.100
A margin divides profit by sales, so you can compare months of different sizes.

19
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:50.590
Here is Funke's October. She opened with stock worth 95000, bought 310000 more, and closed with 80250.

20
00:02:51.840 --> 00:03:00.330
Her sales were 412000 naira. So her cost of goods sold is 324750.

21
00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:08.130
Gross profit is 87250, a gross margin of 21.2%.

22
00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:13.540
Rent share, transport, phone data and power come to 50000.

23
00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:27.590
Net profit is 37250 naira. Of every 100 naira of sales, about 9 naira is net profit. That is up 6250 on September.

24
00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.960
Running costs like rent and transport go in operating expenses.

25
00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:47.770
But money you take out for yourself or your household is not a business expense. Record it as Drawings and leave it out. Otherwise the report hides how much the business really earns, and whether it can afford to pay you.

26
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.610
Put all your tabs in one workbook, and keep a simple routine.

27
00:03:52.960 --> 00:04:01.810
Daily, 5 to 10 minutes, record every sale and expense. Weekly, run your check cell, look at the Reorder list and chase unpaid sales.

28
00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:10.270
Monthly, count your shelves, make the profit report and download a backup. Quarterly, look at three months together and make one decision.

29
00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:19.300
When you share, choose the lowest access that works. Viewer can only look. Give Editor only to people who really need to type.

30
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:24.800
Send a lender or partner the report as a PDF, not every customer's name.

31
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:30.100
If a helper stops working with you, remove their access that same day.

32
00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:45.470
To remember. Closing stock is opening plus in minus sold. A reorder level makes your shopping list. VLOOKUP needs FALSE. Net profit is gross profit minus running costs. And keep drawings out of expenses.

33
00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:55.380
Now build your inventory sheet, make your first monthly profit report as a PDF, and assemble your complete workbook with your own routine.

34
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.670
Continue with the lessons below.
